# Citation File Format 1.2.0.
# `preferred-citation` is the paper. The top-level metadata is the software.

cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  Cite the paper for the findings, and this repository as well if you reuse the
  probes.
title: >-
  Probe suite and measurements for a fully on-premises speech assistant
abstract: >-
  Measurement scripts and raw result files behind the numbers reported in
  "Nothing Leaves the Room: Measuring a Fully On-Premises Speech Assistant and
  Its Failure Modes": latency, interruption reaction, word error rate against
  mixed noise, phantom-turn filtering, per-query energy, and network
  confinement.
type: software
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-09-19
# Code is MIT; the result files, query texts and manifest are CC BY 4.0.
license:
  - MIT
  - CC-BY-4.0
license-url: https://github.com/ttz-leipheim/onprem-speech-assistant-measurements/blob/main/LICENSE
repository-code: https://github.com/ttz-leipheim/onprem-speech-assistant-measurements
url: https://github.com/ttz-leipheim/onprem-speech-assistant-measurements
keywords:
  - on-premises speech assistant
  - barge-in
  - latency measurement
  - open-microphone robustness
  - privacy-preserving deployment
  - research artifact

